.TH "GLESHA-RUN" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glesha-run \- create and upload a full or incremental backup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glesha run SET [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create and upload a full or incremental backup.
.PP
Creates a full backup by default. \-\-incremental requires an existing baseline. Repeating a pending run resumes it with the original archive passphrase.
.PP
Chunked runs use \-\-spool\-max and do not accept \-\-output or \-\-keep\-archive.
.PP
With \-\-from or \-\-to, only their combined bucket selection may be accessed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-full
Create a full snapshot.
.TP
.B \-\-incremental
Create changes relative to an existing baseline.
.TP
.B \-\-output FILE
New output file.
.SS Buckets
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Destination remotes; comma\-separated or repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Source or catalog buckets this command may access.
.TP
.B \-\-prefix PREFIX
Prefix for new archive names: glesha or encb.
.SS Archive settings
.TP
.B \-\-chunked
Upload independent chunks using bounded temporary storage.
.TP
.B \-\-spool\-max SIZE
Maximum temporary chunk payload storage (default 128MiB).
.TP
.B \-\-compression FORMAT
Archive compression: xz, gzip, or bzip2.
.TP
.B \-\-compression\-level LEVEL
Compression level 1..9.
.TP
.B \-\-archive\-mode MODE
Archive memory mode: auto, memory, or stream.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-archive
Retain the local archive after a successful backup.
.SS Passphrases
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE|\-
Catalog passphrase file; '\-' reads stdin.
.TP
.B \-\-passphrase\-file FILE|\-
Archive passphrase file; '\-' reads stdin.
.SS Cloud retrieval
.TP
.B \-\-storage\-class CLASS
AWS storage class.
.SS Performance
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory budget, e.g. 128MiB.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs, \-\-transfer\-workers N
Maximum parallel transfers; memory may lower this limit.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-workers N
Maximum parallel file hashing workers.
.SS Confirmations
.TP
.B \-\-assume\-yes
Skip confirmation prompts for this command.
.SS Global options
.TP
.B \-\-format FORMAT
Result format: plain or json; status also supports table and csv (default: plain).
.TP
.B \-\-progress MODE
Progress on stderr: auto, plain, or off (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-\-config FILE
TOML settings file.
.TP
.B \-\-state\-dir DIR
Local state directory; overrides catalog.directory.
.TP
.B \-\-env FILE
Load credentials; existing process variables take priority.
.TP
.B \-\-color MODE
Color mode: auto, yes, or no (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-L, \-\-log\-level LEVEL
Diagnostic verbosity: debug, info, warn, error, or silent (default: info).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show this command's help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version and build revision.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha run docs
glesha run docs \-\-incremental
.fi
.SH OUTPUT
Results and tables go to stdout. Activity, prompts, warnings, and errors go to stderr.
Use \-\-format=json for version 2 result records, one per line.
JSON diagnostics and progress use separate version 1 records on stderr; neither stream contains ANSI controls.
Use \-\-progress=off to disable progress. In plain output, redirected stderr or TERM=dumb uses step lines.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1)
